# Every shell script in this repo is executed inside a Linux container
# (docker-entrypoint-initdb.d, gate-bundle/run-container.sh, the Woodpecker
# pipeline steps) or by a POSIX shell directly. Checked out on a Windows
# machine with the common `core.autocrlf=true`, a script with no
# .gitattributes entry is silently converted to CRLF line endings on
# checkout -- which breaks its shebang the instant something Linux-side
# tries to run it ("/bin/sh^M: bad interpreter: No such file or directory").
# Confirmed live: this took down compose/minimal's own Postgres
# initialization step (init-multi-db.sh) on first launch from a fresh
# Windows checkout.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf

# YAML pipeline definitions are parsed by Woodpecker server-side; keep them
# byte-stable across platforms rather than relying on every tool involved
# tolerating CRLF.
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# Config Terraform reads and Rego policy, same reasoning.
*.tf text eol=lf
*.rego text eol=lf

# This file exists specifically to stop CRLF creeping into checked-out
# scripts and config; without its own rule it would be exposed to exactly
# that on the next checkout.
.gitattributes text eol=lf

# Keep vendored front-end assets and font licence texts byte-identical so their
# recorded sha256 stays valid on Windows checkouts.
portal/web/static/vendor/** -text
portal/web/static/fonts/** -text
*.woff2 binary
